1
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:35,500
This temple was built around the time Ancient Kyoto was established,

2
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:40,000
and was originally called Takaosan-ji Temple.

3
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:47,500
Residing here was Kobo Daishi, Kukai.

4
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,500
which led to the temple being officially named Jingo-kokuso-shingon -ji.

5
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The true magnificence of this Jingo-ji Temple really hits you when come here.

6
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,500
It was a place I'd long yearned to visit.

7
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:16,000
The opportunity to perform here thanks to my connection with Taro,

8
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,500
and the chance to experience this truly special moment,

9
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:25,000
has been an incredibly significant experience for me.

10
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:22,500
Taro-san makes such a wonderful painting.

11
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:27,500
While the painting itself is very wild,

12
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,500
the temple that left such a impression on Taro's mind

13
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:35,000
he's been visiting here for a long time, and that sparked his inspiration for the painting.

14
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,500
So when I suggested, "Wouldn't it be nice to write some calligraphy too?

15
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:42,000
he said, "Please join in,

16
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:47,000
and that's how I came to participate this time.

17
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:09,500
This painting features a wolf or a fox-like figure, incredibly powerful

18
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:13,000
This great piece is such a wild, powerful painting.

19
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:19,500
So, conversely I thought about stillness.

20
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:24,500
About quiet observation. About gazing quietly.

21
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:28,500
When he was painting, the people around him were truly quiet,

22
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,500
They were intently watching the music and Taro's brushwork.

23
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:41,500
Well, (it means) by quietly observing

24
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:47,500
you sort out your own heart and rediscover your true self.

25
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,500
I felt that opportunity was born this time,

26
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:52,500
so I was inspired to write those characters.

27
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
It's an amazing sensation.

28
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,500
the moment when a groove is born.

29
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:27,500
That moment when each element seems to blend together.

30
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:30,500
That experience is incredibly fascinating.

31
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:35,500
I'm looking forward to discovering how the sound changes in other places.

32
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:26,500
After Taro painted,

33
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:30,500
It was a true honor to be able to add my calligraphy

34
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:37,500
It was truly wonderful, with the flute, guitar, and piano being played all around us.

35
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:40,500
As it matched the music so perfectly,

36
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:46,000
I said, "If there's another chance like this, I'd love to collaborate again.

37
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:52,500
I'm incredibly happy to have been part of such a performance.

38
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:55,500
An experience like this doesn't come along often in life, and it made truely happy.

39
00:07:55,500 --> 00:08:02,000
I'm also incredibly proud that Chief Priest Taniuchi participated.

40
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:07,000
It's not something you can easily ask for, and it's not something you experience often, even as an artist.

41
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,000
learned a lot from the priest too

42
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,000
While deeply feeling the spirit of Kyoto

43
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:21,500
I was overjoyed to do live art right here in front of The Deity of Protection.
